  "flag_reading": [
    "A flag is kind:field:cause, and the field is the value whose status the flag describes, by its schemas/risk-scoring.yaml name: cvss_base, composite_score, severity_band, remediation_sla, risk_disposition, review_date, reachability.",
    "The cause of a 'corrected' flag names the step that produced the field's new value: a changed cvss_base is 'vector', a changed composite_score is 'arithmetic', a changed severity_band is 'band-mapping' (or 'rounding' when only rounding moved the band), and a changed remediation_sla, risk_disposition or review_date is 'follows-band'. Where a fallback set the review date, 'baseline-date' or 'clock-restarted' replaces 'follows-band'. A change that the asset tags alone explain takes 'retagged' and the cause 'asset-tags' on every field it moves (ruling A). A finding carries at most one flag per kind and field.",
    "A rounding-only composite difference is normalized and counted and never flagged: only a band that it moves is flagged, as severity_band:rounding.",
    "basis 'pinned': the string is in the closed vocabulary of contracts/module-signatures.md, and a test requires it. 'optional': the renderer may add the flag or not, and a test accepts both. Only the flags on a value that the input's form lacks are optional, because the cause for those is open (S-12(b), named by T032).",
    "A flag that the renderer adds and that is not listed is a defect of one side: the list is complete for the cases here."
  ],
  "notes": [
    "The baseline is a renderer-form (schema 1.1) risk-scores.md: it records each row's assessed vector, its score_bounds, the tags it was scored under and its scored-on date in Section 6's Scoring Inputs (the format frozen in contracts/module-signatures.md). So every case here is decidable: recomputing with the recorded tags either gives the stored value (a retag) or it does not (a correction).",
    "Ruling A, up: a tag added on vector-store-a (pii) raises the score and the band. The change is retagged, never corrected, for the CVSS score, the composite, the band and the values that follow the band. The review date becomes this run's date plus the new SLA unless the stored review date is earlier ('up-band-review-later' and 'up-band-review-earlier'). An SLA override keeps its review date and its SLA ('up-band-sla-override'); the disposition still follows the band.",
    "Ruling A, down: the financial tag on audit-ledger is gone, so the score and the band fall. The original scoring date is kept, so the review date is the scored-on date plus the lower band's SLA ('down-band'). A deadline missed under the lower band stays missed.",
    "PM-T7: 'band-holds-tag-added' and 'band-holds-tag-removed' move cvss_base and the composite but not the band: both are flagged retagged, the band is not flagged, and nothing that follows the band changes.",
    "R-25's documented outcomes are controls, flagged zero times: an assessed score above 9.2 that the tag does not lower, an elevated score that the 9.2 ceiling holds at 9.2, a tag whose bits the vector already has, a tag that was already in effect when the row was scored, an untagged finding, and a NEW finding's score held at its category bound (stored as score_bounds).",
    "Reachability is the trusted-zone value (2.5) with no barriers, as the renderer computes it from the recorded zone, trust level and barrier counts. The Section 6 narrative rows hold plain prose with no numeral and no slot.",
    "The run's threats.md carries the populator's Affected Assets block for this architecture, so it is a fixed point of the populator."
  ],
